# Inactive Omni template fragment: not included by kustomization.yaml.
# Activation requires a newly registered Omni machine UUID, reviewed seccomp
# profile, and successful disposable sandbox probe. Do not use a CP UUID.
#
# VM candidate (inventory checked 2026-10-18): pve, 2 vCPU, 4096 MiB fixed RAM,
# 32 GiB disk on local_storage, virtio NIC on vmbr0, no host/data-disk mounts.
# Allocate VMID immediately before creation; reserve DHCP/IP before boot.
# pve had 15.78 GiB available RAM, local_storage had 1.55 TiB free (thin).
#
# Boot NEW Omni-generated Talos v1.14.4 amd64 ISO from omni.f4mily.net.
# Existing talos-v1.13.2-nocloud-amd64.iso does not enroll into Omni.
# ISO includes SideroLink registration material: keep private, unmount after
# installation, delete temporary media/preset when no longer needed.
# Obtain UUID from Omni after registration, verify it against VM SMBIOS UUID.
# Add that UUID under the existing Workers.machines and append this Machine
# document to cluster-template.yaml. Do not create a second Workers document.
# Never apply old OpenTofu homelab-kube env: it also writes machine config.
#
# REQUIRED before activation: machine.seccompProfiles entry ainsel-codex.json
# with a reviewed default-deny profile derived from containerd v2.3.7 for
# capabilities.drop ALL; preserve clone3 ENOSYS fallback. Trace Codex/bwrap
# on disposable worker before allowing additional namespace/mount syscalls.
# Keep SELinux enabled; investigate AVC denials independently from seccomp.
# Talos v1.14.4 policy currently grants user_namespace create explicitly only
# to pod_containerd_t. A normal pod may fail in enforcing mode. Verify actual
# SecurityState (default is permissive per Talos docs) and auditd AVC logs;
# enforcing support needs a reviewed policy solution before activation.
# Profile must appear at /var/lib/kubelet/seccomp/profiles/ainsel-codex.json.
#
# Do NOT place protected label in KubeNodeConfig.labels. After a secret-free
# sandbox smoke test, a cluster administrator grants the admission marker:
# kubectl label node talos-codex1 \
#   ainsel.dev.node-restriction.kubernetes.io/codex-sandbox=true
# AInsel sandboxProfile codex requires that marker, the toleration below,
# and Localhost profiles/ainsel-codex.json. Missing prerequisites fail closed.
# Remove marker first for rollback; drain Jobs before removing the worker
# from Omni template. Destroying its VM/disk is a separate destructive step.
#
# References:
# https://docs.siderolabs.com/omni/omni-cluster-setup/registering-machines/register-a-bare-metal-machine-iso
# https://docs.siderolabs.com/kubernetes-guides/security/seccomp-profiles
# https://docs.siderolabs.com/talos/v1.14/reference/configuration/runtime/sysctlconfig
# https://docs.siderolabs.com/talos/v1.14/reference/configuration/kubernetes/kubenodeconfig
# https://docs.siderolabs.com/talos/v1.14/security/selinux
kind: Machine
name: REPLACE_WITH_NEW_OMNI_MACHINE_UUID
patches:
  - idOverride: 200-codex-sandbox-worker
    annotations:
      name: codex-sandbox-worker
    inline: |
      apiVersion: v1alpha1
      kind: HostnameConfig
      hostname: talos-codex1
      auto: 'off'
      ---
      apiVersion: v1alpha1
      kind: SysctlConfig
      params:
        user.max_user_namespaces: "1024"
      ---
      apiVersion: v1alpha1
      kind: KubeNodeConfig
      taints:
        ainsel.dev/sandbox: codex:NoSchedule
      ---
      apiVersion: v1alpha1
      kind: KubeletConfig
      defaultRuntimeSeccompProfileEnabled: true
